      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you are not safe to wait, sleep, or take over-the-counter medication at all right now, as the combination of sudden severe headache, vision loss, and one-sided limb weakness is a classic sign of a stroke. Even if you have had similar symptoms before, those episodes typically do not involve the lasting loss of vision and limb weakness seen today. Please call emergency services immediately; the only way to save your life or disability from potential brain damage is to get to a hospital now, regardless of cost or wait times.",
